# Strip AI metadata from generated images

After creating any image (GenerateImage, canvas export, screenshot composite, or similar), **remove AI provenance metadata** before treating the file as done.

## Do this every time

1. Save the image to disk.
2. Run:

```bash
node scripts/strip-image-metadata.mjs <path-to-image>
```

3. If several files were created, pass the folder.

The script drops JPEG EXIF/XMP/IPTC/C2PA/comment segments and PNG text chunks, without changing the picture.

## Scope

Applies to Instagram graphics, branded assets, and any other generated image the user may download or post — in the repo (`public/`) or Cursor assets folders.

Do not skip this because the file "looks clean." C2PA and XMP are invisible in Preview.
